; ===============  linux
## rtfm man pages
; RTFM means "read the manual". Every Linux command and function has a man page.
; Read it first: it is the real answer, written by the people who made the tool.
man PAGE                           # read the manual page of a command or function  @rtfm @help @docs  <man:man(1)>
https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/  # read Linux man pages online (commands, syscalls, libc)  @rtfm @manpages @docs  <https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/>
; Search in man:
apropos -s 2 .            # every syscall page
apropos -s 7 . | less     # browse all overview pages
apropos -a access control # pages whose description contains both words

